**Database Selection**
**Technical Requirement**
1.Transaction Integrity & ACID Compliance:When a stock trade is carried out, it is necessary to update various factors all at once such as the cash balance of the
user, stock available for sale, portfolio holdings as well as auditing trails. These steps are interdependent; hence if one of them fails, it will lead to 
instant rollback of the whole process in order to avoid imbalance errors.
2.Data Model:In this domain, there are clear and distinct entities that have high level of relationships. They include Users, Stocks, Portfolios, Transactions 
as well as System Logs. These entities have specified relationships involving one-to-many or many-to-many links.
3.Concurrency and thread handling:Under multi-threaded user activity, concurrent buy/sell execution requires row-level locking or isolated transactions to avoid race 
conditions and double-spending errors.

**Considerations of MongoDB**: Although MongoDB provides high writing speed and flexible document nature which is appropriate for crude market price feed, 
it is not enough. Additional application level enforcing and replica sets arrangement is necessary while handling financial relationships as well as cross documents 
consistencies.

**Advantage of MySQL**: The storage engine InnoDB of MySQL has an inbuilt ACID compliance, immediate consistency, explicit foreign keys referential integrity and 
standard row level locking mechanism. It is for this reason that such capabilities of MySQL conform to requirements of monetary transactions as well as the 
evaluation of DBMS in academic researches.
